    named above rather than counted. A workflow is judged on its last 3
    scheduled runs whenever they happened, so a firing delay cannot skew it.
    DEAD means none of those 3 runs worked: each failed, was skipped, or never
    started (startup_failure). A window holding anything else — a success, or
    cancelled, timed_out, action_required, neutral — is counted healthy above.
